## `story.ni:4837`

define phrase shannon-see-mrs-sandler
  'I suppose we should go see Mrs. Sandler now,' Shannon says.
end phrase

## `story.ni:10069`, the goodbye; then the step into Sandler & Sons.

define phrase shannon-goodbye-hug
  'Well,' says Shannon, 'I've seen you safely to Dame Sandler. I'd better get
  back to Maiden House; the Baron's men might get suspicious if I'm gone too
  long. Take care, Jacqueline.' She hugs you tightly, sniffling a little, and
  then hurries off to the south.
end phrase

## `story.ni:10111`

define phrase reluctant-to-break-silence
  Something about this place — the stillness, the solemn expectancy — makes
  you reluctant to break the silence with idle chatter.
end phrase

