## The bookshelves' paragraph (`story.ni:10344-10349`): the long one on the
## first look, the short one after, none once the box is down.

define phrase shelves-and-the-box, stopping while the wooden box is shelved
  The empty shelves are bowed slightly, permanently warped from spending so
  many years supporting the weight of as many books as they could hold. And
  beneath the dust, the wood is worn, scuffed — a sign that those books were
  not merely for show, but taken down and read, again and again. It occurs
  to you that the Duke must have loved his books. You're not sure why you are
  so certain of this, but certain you are. Of all the desecrations visited
  upon his home since his death, you think this room would have made him the
  saddest.

  Up on the top shelf, missed by the looters, you spy a wooden box.
or
  Nearly hidden on one of the top bookshelves is a wooden box.
end phrase

create the dusty bookshelves
  aka bookshelves, shelves, shelf, bookshelf, top shelf, topmost shelf, empty shelves, looted shelves, warped shelves
  scenery, plural
  in the Office

  The bookshelves have been completely looted.

  on the player examining
    refuse when the wooden box is shelved: shelves-except-the-box
  end on

  on the player climbing
    refuse box-out-of-reach
  end on

define phrase shelves-except-the-box
  The bookshelves have been completely looted, except for a wooden box
  almost hidden up on the topmost shelf.
end phrase

