## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the Red Gate Third Floor Landing
  a room
  aka landing, third floor landing, top of the stairs
  down to the Red Gate Second Floor Landing
  south to the Red Gate Master Bedroom

  The stairs end here at the third floor. A doorway leads south.

create the Red Gate Master Bedroom
  a room
  aka bedroom, master bedroom, duke's bedroom, duke's room
  north to the Red Gate Third Floor Landing
  south to the Bathroom
  first time
    Most of the furniture from this room has been carted off. Only the bed
    remains, just a bare mattress covered with yet another plain, dusty
    sheet. Doorways lead north and south.

    Even before the events of the last two days, you had heard of the Duke,
    of course. And although there are many theories about exactly what
    brought him low — illness; treachery; heartbreak when his wife, the
    Duchess, left him — all agree that he passed away in his sleep. This,
    then, is where he died. This very room, in this very bed. This mattress,
    cold, stripped, and covered with dust, is the closest in time you will
    ever come to the man who was your father, the Duke of Toresal.

    And Bobby is dead now, too. And maybe Widow Fiona and Widow Shannon, if
    the Baron figures out that they helped me. And who else then? Teisha?
    Olmer and Darrens? All because of this stupid letter... I never asked for
    this.

    You close your eyes for a moment, fighting off a dreadful sense of
    futility.

  Most of the furniture from this room has been carted off. Only the bed
  remains, just a bare mattress covered with yet another plain, dusty sheet.
  Doorways lead north and south.

create the bare bed
  aka bed, mattress, bare mattress, duke's bed, dusty sheet, plain sheet
  scenery
  in the Red Gate Master Bedroom

  No one has slept in it since the Duke died, years ago.

  on the player searching
    refuse more-dust-under-the-bed
  end on

  on the player entering
    refuse bare-mattress-no-comfort
  end on

  on the player climbing
    refuse bare-mattress-no-comfort
  end on

define phrase more-dust-under-the-bed
  Nothing under there but more dust.
end phrase

define phrase bare-mattress-no-comfort
  It would hardly be comfortable, lying on a bare mattress in this forlorn,
  empty house.
end phrase

